{"term":"mediate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6cc293a682afacdde1","definition":"To resolve differences, or to bring about a settlement, between conflicting parties.","example":"Negotiators managed to mediate a ceasefire.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8abfe999aea3f7e9a9","definition":"To intervene between conflicting parties in order to resolve differences or bring about a settlement.","example":"\"Nay,\" replied Charles, gravely, \"this is carrying your anger too far. Allow me to mediate between you. I must entreat, nay, I command, the Lady Francesca's presence.\"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9f8667d6a99b25abf7","definition":"To divide into two equal parts.","example":"Then, Meaſuring Land, by vvalking over it, they ſtyled a Double-ſtep (i.e. the Space from the elevation of one Foot, to the ſame Foot ſet dovvn again, mediated by a ſtep of the other Foot) a Pace, equal to 5 Foot; a Thouſand of vvhich Paces made a Mile, vvhich is a Meaſure ſerving for any diſtance on Earth, and even for the Height of the Sphears.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7bce4ed7fee38159fb","definition":"To act as an intermediary causal or communicative agent; to convey.","example":"He had some advantage in the difference of our weapons; for his sword, as I recollect, was longer than mine, […] His obvious malignity of purpose never for a moment threw him off his guard, and he exhausted every feint and strategem proper to the science of defence; while, at the same time, he mediated the most desperate catastrophe to our rencounter.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aed77bf6dbfafabd5c","definition":"To act as a spiritualistic medium.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ec2decc96b9f17d3e9","definition":"To communicate via media; to frame; to provide a cultural narrative about.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2ac2a1fd663e6b3ff8","definition":"Acting through a mediating agency, indirect.","example":"The Leibnitzio-Wolfians distinguish three acts in the process of representative cognition: — 1° the act of representing a (mediate) object to the mind; 2° the representation, or, to speak more properly, representamen, itself as an (immediate or vicarious) object exhibited to the mind; 3° the act by which the mind is conscious, immediately of the representative object, and, through it, mediately of the remote object represented.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated","mediately","mediateness"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:719dd159319f9b2c18","definition":"Intermediate between extremes.","example":"soon the mediate clouds shall be dispell'd","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated","mediately","mediateness"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:15740aaffb288d4a78","definition":"Gained or effected by a medium or condition.","example":"mediate positive proof","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated","mediately","mediateness"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈmidieɪt/"},"wordFamily":["antibody-mediated rejection","electromediated","hypermediated","immunomediate","mediatable","mediatingly","mediative","nonmediated","nonmediating","telemediated","unmediated","mediately","mediateness"]}